2	 "gdd": "design/gdd/web-map-and-transit.md",
3	 "blockers": [
4	  {
5	   "where": "WM-31 (L299), event table rows POD_DEPARTED/DERELICT_LOADED (L303, L305), AC-WM-57 (L1616) vs WM-36 / AC-WM-60 (L319, L1622) and WM-3",
6	   "issue": "The sync tells Attention and Horror to 'read web.state's view in their hooks' (departure, and 'the dormancy flags'), but no such read surface exists in this GDD. WM-36's web.view has an exact, negatively asserted field list (AC-WM-60) with no departure or dormancy member. Dormancy lives in graph.state (see AC-WM-56). An implementer cannot tell what Attention and Horror read in place of POD_DEPARTED and DERELICT_LOADED/UNLOADED, and an exact-list AC forbids adding one to web.view.",
7	   "fix": "Name the read each consumer uses: either existing members (transit_state, leg_target_id and leg_dir give departure; Graph's dormant flag gives dormancy, cited as the read) or a new explicit member. If one is added, extend WM-36 and AC-WM-60 so the exact-list assertion stays true."
8	  },
9	  {
10	   "where": "WM-30 (L297), WM-3 machine fields (L199), D.11 machine_bytes 125 and the 756 B total (L738, L742), AC-WM-75, AC-WM-59",
11	   "issue": "pod_arrived_seq and berthed_seq are introduced only as a 'web.state read view' requirement in WM-31 and AC-WM-57. They are not in the WM-3 field list, the state_hash row, the byte budget or the persisted/not-persisted split of WM-30. Whether they are block fields (persisted, hashed, in the golden save, +8 B or more) or derived or non-persisted is undefined, and so is when they advance (in the pod_settle and last berth_step applies, keyed to the nominal tick). Two implementers would build different schemas, and AC-WM-57 and the byte and golden-save ACs would then disagree.",
12	   "fix": "Add one rule in WM-3 or WM-30: either the two counters are u32 block fields, persisted, in state_hash and counted in D.11 (update machine_bytes, the 756 B figure, the golden save and AC-WM-75), or they are non-persisted read-view members that start at 0 on restore. State that they increment in the apply that sets the event, and that Save/Load re-reads its last-seen values after a load (ADR-0006 1.12)."
13	  }
